                  "text": "Hello! I am the **Medicaid Application Auditor**. \n\n### **My Role & Mission**\nMy core mission is to audit and analyze Medicaid application data extracts to detect highly suspicious, anomalous, or potentially fraudulent submissions. I evaluate both individual anomalies and cross-row matching patterns to flag application risks.\n\n---\n\n### **Data I Analyze**\nI analyze Medicaid application records stored in Google BigQuery:\n* **Project ID:** `ai-hub-459714`\n* **Dataset:** `frauddector`\n* **Table:** `syntheticdatafraud`\n\n---\n\n### **Core Detection Rules & Patterns**\nI audit the dataset against key fraud and anomaly indicators, including:\n\n1. **Credential Recycling:** Shared or identical `PASSWORD` or `USERNAME` across multiple distinct `NUM_CASE` entries.\n2. **Address Clustering:** More than two distinct `NUM_CASE` records sharing the exact same street address (`ADR_STREET_1`).\n3. **Identity Mismatches:** Discrepancies where applicant names (`NAM_FIRST` / `NAM_LAST`) do not align with their `USERNAME`, `EMAIL_ADDRESS` prefix, or password patterns.\n4. **Sequential Clusters:** Incremental numeric sequences appearing in `ADR_STREET_1`, `EMAIL_ADDRESS`, `USERNAME`, or `PASSWORD`.\n5. **Pregnant Member Clustering:** Records sharing the same first name (`NAM_FIRST`) and birth year (`DTE_BIRTH`) with a relationship/category code of `CNF` (pregnant member).\n\n---\n\nFeel free to ask me to run an audit across all rules, investigate a specific anomaly pattern, or query specific records in the dataset!",
